(Section 6. Haulage Operations) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6.1 Haulage is performed by prime movers with 20ft or 40ft trailers. The verified gross mass of) Tj T*
(a container on our trailers must not exceed 25,000 kg, in line with the Association of) Tj T*
(Malaysian Hauliers limit at Port Klang. Overweight containers must be re-stuffed or moved with) Tj T*
(a special permit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6.2 Drivers must complete a pre-trip inspection covering tyres, brakes, lights, twist locks and) Tj T*
(the container seal number before leaving the port.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6.3 Rail \(KTMB intermodal\) is offered for Ipoh and Prai \(Penang\). For distances above 200 km,) Tj T*
(planners must quote both truck and rail options so the customer can compare cost and emissions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6.4 Shipments to Sabah and Sarawak travel by coastal shipping from Port Klang. Delivery inside) Tj T*
(East Malaysia is subcontracted to partner hauliers and quoted separately.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Section 7. Demurrage, Detention and Storage) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7.1 Demurrage is charged by the shipping line when a full container stays in the port beyond) Tj T*
(the free time. Detention is charged when the customer keeps the container outside the port) Tj T*
(beyond the free days before returning it empty.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7.2 Typical free time at Port Klang is 3 days for port storage and 5 to 7 days for container) Tj T*
(detention, depending on the shipping line. Always confirm the free time on the delivery order.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7.3 The planning team reviews all containers daily. Any container within one day of its free) Tj T*
(time expiring must be escalated to the Operations Manager and prioritised for collection or) Tj T*
(return.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Section 8. Warehousing) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8.1 Storage is charged per pallet per day, and handling is charged per pallet for receiving and) Tj T*
(dispatch. Dangerous goods stored in the DG warehouse are charged at 1.8 times the general) Tj T*
(storage rate.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8.2 Stock must be managed first-in-first-out \(FIFO\), except palm-based products with batch) Tj T*
(expiry dates, which use first-expired-first-out \(FEFO\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8.3 Cycle counts are carried out weekly for DG stock and monthly for general cargo. Inventory) Tj T*
(variance above 0.5 percent must be investigated within 48 hours.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Section 9. Quotations and Pricing) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(9.1 Quotations are built from the company rate card: diesel \(updated weekly from the Ministry) Tj T*
(of Finance retail price\), truck maintenance per kilometre, fixed truck cost and driver time per) Tj T*
(hour, tolls, port handling charges, customs fees, cargo surcharges and warehousing.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(9.2 The standard margin on cost is 15 percent. Discounts above 5 percent require approval from) Tj T*
(the Commercial Manager.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
